diff --git a/docs/architecture/native-acceptance.md b/docs/architecture/native-acceptance.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7ff905b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/architecture/native-acceptance.md
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Native acceptance procedure (T09 and chunk native assertions)
+
+`xtask native --chunk Cxx` builds the fixture-identity app with
+`native-prepare` and records its executable SHA-256. Acceptance is a separate
+record, `docs/planning/evidence/Cxx/native-acceptance.json`
+(schema `airs-v2/native-acceptance/1`, parsed strictly by xtask), produced by
+actually driving that exact executable:
+
+- `method: "cua"` — automation through macOS accessibility/automation APIs
+  against the real native window (for example REA native UI capture or System
+  Events), with the captured accessibility trees/screenshots stored under
+  `evidence/Cxx/native/`; or
+- `method: "operator"` — a person performs the checklist on the real app and
+  records observations per check.
+
+Every check must report `pass` with an observation and evidence paths. A
+`fail` or `blocked` check, a record naming different executable bytes, or a
+record for the production identity fails the gate. Build success, mocked IPC
+tests or reviewer scores never substitute for this record.
+
+Prerequisites on the acceptance host: macOS grants the automation client
+**Accessibility** (to read the AX tree and send key events) and, for
+screenshots, **Screen Recording**. Without these grants automated acceptance is
+blocked; the operator method remains available.
+
+## C01 checklist
+
+| ID | Check |
+|---|---|
+| C01-N01 | Fixture app launches from the bundle; window title "Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 (Fixture)"; build identity shows "Fixture build". |
+| C01-N02 | Native menus exist: app menu (About, Settings… ⌘,, Hide, Quit), Edit, View (Command Palette… ⌘K, Appearance), Go (feature destinations ⌘1–⌘9), Window. |
+| C01-N03 | Keyboard only: Tab reaches the Features navigation; Enter on a destination moves focus to its page heading and marks it current; visible focus ring on every stop. |
+| C01-N04 | ⌘K opens the palette with focus in the field; typing filters; Enter navigates; Escape closes and restores focus to the previously focused control. |
+| C01-N05 | Go menu shortcuts (e.g. ⌘2 Academy, ⌘, Settings) navigate through the native menu → observation channel path. |
+| C01-N06 | Every product destination shows "not available in this build" with its planned chunk; none presents data or contacts a service. |
+| C01-N07 | Settings → Appearance: Light/Dark/Match System change the shared theme only after the native snapshot arrives; View → Appearance does the same. |
+| C01-N08 | Accessibility tree: navigation landmark "Features", buttons with names including "Not available in this build" where applicable, `aria-current` reflected as selected/current, headings exposed in reading order (the inputs VoiceOver uses). |
+| C01-N09 | Window resizing to the minimum (900×600) keeps the rail, topbar and content usable without overlap. |
+| C01-N10 | Startup makes no network connection (see evidence/C01/native/startup-network.json). |
+| C01-N11 | No Academy learner/gamification element (XP, credits, streak, notifications) appears on general screens. |
+
+VoiceOver speech itself is verified by reading the same accessibility
+attributes it consumes; a spoken-output transcript is a C24 cumulative item
+unless recorded earlier by an operator.
